Ownership of a DMA buffer Figure description and sources <p>Three states. A buffer is constructed in Cpu: static, line-aligned and padded. Lend moves it from Cpu to Device after the owned cache lines are cleaned or invalidated and a barrier ran. Complete moves it from Device back to Cpu after a receive is invalidated and a barrier ran; Abort with proof that the bus master stopped also returns it to Cpu. Abort without proof, or a lease destroyed while the device owns the buffer, moves it from Device to Quarantined. Recover with proof, after the peripheral was re-initialised, moves it from Quarantined to Cpu. In Quarantined a Lend is refused with a Fault and the CPU view is empty. Only the port holds the key that moves a buffer between states (ADR-0030).</p> <p>Drawn from: <code>docs/model/dma-lease.state.yml</code>.</p> <p>A <code>Buffer</code> is a static object: aligned to its region's unit, padded to a whole number of units, so cache maintenance over it never reaches a neighbour. <code>CpuView()</code> returns the data while the CPU owns the buffer and an empty span otherwise (counted in <code>Stats().cpu_denied</code>). The port moves it with a <code>PortKey</code>, a passkey only the port's own class can construct:</p> <pre><code>Lease&lt;Region&gt; lease;
buffer.Lend(key, Direction::FromDevice, used, ops, lease);   // clean + invalidate the owned lines, barrier
// ... program the DMA with lease.DeviceView(key) ...
lease.Complete(key, ops, Outcome::Ok);                        // invalidate, barrier, the CPU owns it again
</code></pre> Call Result <code>Lend</code> <code>Ok</code>; <code>InvalidArgument</code> (bad length, or the lease is already active); <code>Busy</code> (on the device); <code>Fault</code> (quarantined) <code>Complete</code> Memory back to the CPU; <code>InvalidArgument</code> for an inactive lease <code>Abort(Confirmed)</code> Memory back to the CPU: the port saw the enable bit read 0 <code>Abort(NotConfirmed)</code> <code>Fault</code>, the buffer is quarantined: nobody may touch it while a master may still write <code>Recover</code> Only with proof, after the peripheral was re-initialised destroying an active lease Quarantines the buffer <p>Cache maintenance per policy:</p> Policy Transmit lend Receive lend Receive return <code>Coherent</code>, <code>NonCacheable</code> barrier barrier barrier <code>Maintained</code> clean the used lines clean, then invalidate all owned lines invalidate the used lines <p>The receive lend cleans before it invalidates so that a dirty line cannot be evicted over the data the device is about to write. The default region on a part with a data cache is a non-cacheable block set up by the MPU (ADR-0032).</p>
